#edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050775 #edb/ref 1031 "Properties of Expectation for Discrete Random Variables" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050775 #edb/ref 1033 2836 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050775 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "65bfe855-0363-58b6-a91d-f3f12be3a932" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050965 #edb/ref 1027 #edb/ref 17592186049908 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050965 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186162127 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050965 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186162128 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050965 #edb/ref 1028 #edb/ref 17592186162129 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050965 #edb/ref 1031 "Conditional Expectation for Continuous Random Variables" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050965 #edb/ref 1033 3057 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186050965 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "7619e09a-ee66-5b0d-b62b-731fbe484a0a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186190324 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186190325 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186190324 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186190326 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186190324 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186190327 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186190324 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186190328 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186190324 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186190329 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186190324 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186190324 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186190324 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "dbb35035-e4ad-5dfe-8305-ac38b8d7b733" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186190325 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{4}{5}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186190325 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186190325 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8e870738-b0c3-5a45-a958-0a8ab816e8ac" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186190326 #edb/ref 1080 "4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186190326 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186190326 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a6105e5f-10e9-560d-b7e2-58cef8643cfd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186190327 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186190327 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186190327 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c7b9be8a-5521-5f98-8ff2-7e30822d0744" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186190328 #edb/ref 1080 "6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186190328 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186190328 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "fa218f47-8a14-524f-b582-ac051f2f4b5e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186190329 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{14}{5}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186190329 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186190329 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6095d4ff-1396-56a8-a23b-76ac5552bb6d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192617 #edb/ref 1069 "e-7985" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192617 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\textrm E[X].$\n\n$$\nf(x) = \\dfrac{x^2}{9}, \\quad 0 \\leq x \\leq 3\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192617 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "61c51284-18f0-5398-857b-7687228e8df8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192617 #edb/ref 1074 "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[X] = \\int_S x \\cdot f(x) \\, \\textrm dx\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}x\\cdot \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{3}}{9}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{4}}{36}|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192618 #edb/ref 1069 "e-7986" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192618 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\textrm E[7X-4].$\n\n$$\nf(x) = \\dfrac{3x^2}{7}, \\quad 1 <        x <        2\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192618 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c755eddf-3b0d-5a33-aa13-e6a3f7da4244" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192618 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we simplify using the properties of expected value:\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[7X-4] = 7 \\textrm E[X] - 4\n$$\n\nFor a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm{E}[X] = \\int_S x \\cdot f(x) \\,\\textrm{d}x\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{S}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}x\\cdot \\frac{3{x}^{2}}{7}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{3{x}^{3}}{7}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{3{x}^{4}}{28}|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{45}{28}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[7X-4] & =7\\text{E}[X]-4 \\\\  & =7\\cdot \\frac{45}{28}-4 \\\\  & =\\frac{29}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192619 #edb/ref 1069 "e-7987" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192619 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $X$ is a continuous random variable with the following probability density function, compute $\\textrm E[X].$\n![](images/98/98b997e3016e9ca5538863c3faa19ac017f90e8bcdeba40e09c03aba28c4ace4.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192619 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3a11b9e3-60c8-57f3-8ec6-4ff378d0db62" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192619 #edb/ref 1074 "For a continuous random variable $X$ with probability density function $f(x)$ defined over a set $S,$ we can calculate the expected value using the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\textrm E[X] = \\int_S x \\cdot f(x) \\, \\textrm dx\n$$\n\n \n\nWe compute the expected value of $X$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}x\\cdot f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}x\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}x\\cdot (\\frac{x}{2}-\\frac{3}{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{x}{4}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{3}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{3x}{4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{{x}^{2}}{8}|}_{0}^{2}+{(\\frac{{x}^{3}}{6}-\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{8})|}_{2}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{31}{24} \\\\  & =\\frac{43}{24}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192675 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048317 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192675 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049638 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192675 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186193396 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192675 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186193398 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192675 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186424086 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192675 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186424088 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192675 #edb/ref 1039 "Computing the Mean of a Continuous Random Variable" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192675 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186192617 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192675 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "d3da4448-71cc-5671-8f32-a9f293ad5054" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192676 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050775 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192676 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186193073 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192676 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186193400 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192676 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186424089 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192676 #edb/ref 1039 "Computing the Mean of a Transformed Continuous Random Variable" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192676 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186192618 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192676 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "8322a1ba-7608-53de-88d9-e360ca8025cd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192677 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050215 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192677 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186193397 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186192677 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186193399 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592